@@ -15,3 +15,38 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts and passkeys
+
+Use Node.js 24 or newer. Run `pnpm dev` and open
+`http://localhost:4321/devtools-times/signup`. Account security is available at
+`/devtools-times/account/security` after signing in.
+
+Accounts can be created with a discoverable passkey or with a password. Password
+accounts can add passkeys later. Sign-in with a passkey does not require a username.
+The security page supports adding, renaming, and removing passkeys and explicitly
+reauthenticating. Security changes require verification within the last five minutes.
+Passkey-only accounts must retain at least one passkey. The app does not provide
+account recovery for lost passkeys; enroll a second device or security key.
+
+Authentication now runs in this application rather than the previous external demo
+API. Existing accounts in that external service are not migrated. New local accounts
+use the same username/password forms, with scrypt password hashes and opaque,
+HttpOnly, SameSite session cookies. Passkey private keys and biometric data remain
+with the authenticator; the server stores public keys and signature counters.
+WebAuthn verification uses [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/docs/packages/server).
+
+For deployment, set `AUTH_ORIGIN` to the exact public HTTPS origin (for example,
+`https://news.example.com`, without a path). This fixes the expected origin and RP
+hostname behind a proxy. Passkeys require HTTPS except on localhost, and passkeys
+created on one hostname cannot be used on another. Set `AUTH_DB_PATH` to a writable,
+persistent SQLite path; it defaults to `./data/auth.sqlite`. Back up this database
+and keep it outside public assets. This SQLite implementation is for a single
+application deployment with persistent storage; multiple replicas need a shared
+authentication database. Sessions expire after seven days, challenges after five
+minutes, and authentication requests are rate limited by client IP.
+
+Run `pnpm test` to build and run HTTP integration tests against an isolated temporary
+database. The tests generate real signed software authenticator responses to exercise
+registration, authentication, reauthentication, management, and security rejection
+paths without opening a browser.
